    "catalog:lod": "300",
    "catalog:format": "2",
    "catalog:tags": "basin, cloakroom basin, wall-hung, cloakroom",
    "catalog:note": "Wall-hung cloakroom basin, no pedestal, its rim fixed to the wall. rim 0.85, bottom 0.70. The rim is one D-shaped outline sweep, 0.04 thick, less a circle outline sweep of radius 0.11 for the bowl opening; the bowl below it is a revolve whose outline, in true arcs centred on its axis, has its 0.012 wall, the waste hole the gap at its axis, filled by a metal waste. A waste tail and a bottle trap hang below the bowl with a waste arm to the wall.",
    "catalog:basedOn": "0.45 x 0.35 is a generic practice size, not checked against a published source (unverified); rim 0.85 as the drafting standard wash basin; bowl 0.22 across and 0.14 deep, generic, unverified; EN 14688 not read. Port sizes from the drafting standard (BS EN 12056-2 conventions), unverified",
    "ifc:class": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
    "ifc:predefinedType": "WASHHANDBASIN",
    "ifcClass": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
